# The agent image's build context: an allow-list, `*` and then re-includes,
# because the agent Dockerfile now compiles every tools/<name>/<name>
# executable in its build stage (ADR 0021). The workspace image does not
# need the tool sources and reads the same allow-list the root .dockerignore
# carries; BuildKit prefers this file to the root one when the build context
# is the directory that holds both (#597).
#
# Re-includes are directories rather than globs on purpose:
# internal/agent/instructions.go embeds ego.md, so a `*.go` allow-list would
# drop an embedded asset and break the build.
*
!go.mod
!go.sum
!cmd
!internal
!tools
